{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00009",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Hi, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.04,
      "end_seconds": 8.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.55,
      "end_seconds": 13.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Doctor, uh, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.77,
      "end_seconds": 16.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.54,
      "end_seconds": 22.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I've been dealing with tightness in my chest when I walk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.95,
      "end_seconds": 26.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.1,
      "end_seconds": 28.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.91,
      "end_seconds": 32.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.17,
      "end_seconds": 37.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Oh, it usually comes with tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.91,
      "end_seconds": 43.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 43.83,
      "end_seconds": 49.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.23,
      "end_seconds": 70.53,
      "duration_seconds": 17.3,
      "text": "Oh, uh, I was getting to that! I mean, uh, as for tiredness, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. There's breathlessness on exertion as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.11,
      "end_seconds": 73.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.39,
      "end_seconds": 78.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.48,
      "end_seconds": 83.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Have you had any cough or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.03,
      "end_seconds": 95.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "No, no cough, no pain at rest. I did have a heavy feeling in the left arm at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.59,
      "end_seconds": 99.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Right, and fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.77,
      "end_seconds": 101.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 102.32,
      "end_seconds": 106.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Well, actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.31,
      "end_seconds": 113.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.71,
      "end_seconds": 122.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you had any swelling in the ankles or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.35,
      "end_seconds": 128.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Hmm, no, no swelling in the ankles or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.85,
      "end_seconds": 130.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.94,
      "end_seconds": 133.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.9,
      "end_seconds": 138.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.88,
      "end_seconds": 143.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Okay, so my sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.81,
      "end_seconds": 146.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.71,
      "end_seconds": 172.65,
      "duration_seconds": 24.94,
      "text": "Um, you know, yes, heart disease. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. It's the not knowing that gets to me. Uh, I have high blood pressure, for nearly five years. I did try to ignore it for a while. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.05,
      "end_seconds": 173.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.29,
      "end_seconds": 177.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.09,
      "end_seconds": 179.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.9,
      "end_seconds": 187.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Well, I've had diabetes, yes. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.05,
      "end_seconds": 206.2,
      "duration_seconds": 18.15,
      "text": "Mm. Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.63,
      "end_seconds": 211.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Uh, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.42,
      "end_seconds": 216.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.79,
      "end_seconds": 219.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Um, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.36,
      "end_seconds": 223.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.26,
      "end_seconds": 226.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.65,
      "end_seconds": 230.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.57,
      "end_seconds": 236.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.02,
      "end_seconds": 245.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Uh, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.64,
      "end_seconds": 248.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.94,
      "end_seconds": 261.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "For my blood pressure, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Rosuvastatin. I take it 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 262.19,
      "end_seconds": 271.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Doctor, uh, I think the last prescription for the rosuvastatin was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.82,
      "end_seconds": 279.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.41,
      "end_seconds": 290.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "I, I don't think I have it with me. Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.49,
      "end_seconds": 293.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.93,
      "end_seconds": 296.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.17,
      "end_seconds": 300.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.98,
      "end_seconds": 301.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.77,
      "end_seconds": 319.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.8,
      "end_seconds": 331.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.92,
      "end_seconds": 334.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.75,
      "end_seconds": 346.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Alright, just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.19,
      "end_seconds": 365.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.9, pulse 77, saturation 97 percent. And BP is 158 over 102."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.25,
      "end_seconds": 370.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Uh, um, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.4,
      "end_seconds": 374.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.46,
      "end_seconds": 378.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.92,
      "end_seconds": 379.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.77,
      "end_seconds": 400.29,
      "duration_seconds": 14.52,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. From what you've told me, my working impression is angina-type chest pain. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. It could also be a musculoskeletal cause, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.2,
      "end_seconds": 407.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, you know, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.55,
      "end_seconds": 424.67,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now angina-type chest pain is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk, mild, and no pain at rest or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.66,
      "end_seconds": 427.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.58,
      "end_seconds": 434.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a treadmill test for exertional chest tightness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 435.53,
      "end_seconds": 439.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "We have a slot Thursday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.68,
      "end_seconds": 442.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Thursday, that works for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.1,
      "end_seconds": 467.81,
      "duration_seconds": 23.71,
      "text": "Let's get an echocardiogram, for chest tightness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. It's for chest tightness. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.25,
      "end_seconds": 481.14,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 482.7,
      "end_seconds": 484.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.77,
      "end_seconds": 493.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 494.94,
      "end_seconds": 495.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 499.36,
      "end_seconds": 507.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back. Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 508.53,
      "end_seconds": 520.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "So, I take the GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 521.12,
      "end_seconds": 525.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 526.09,
      "end_seconds": 530.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}